{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":494502,"name":"August Su - TW (SR)","username":"August_Su_TW_SR","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/a/ecd19e/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-18T01:16:00.686Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494502-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494502-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494502-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494502-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003cbr\u003e\nOn first launch after sign-in, Grok Bot briefly shows “Creating Grok Bot’s computer”, then the main window goes fully white/blank. No UI, no Settings, so I can’t use Update/Reset Agent Computer myself. Reinstalling the app, clearing local cache, fully quitting leftover processes, and relaunching does not fix it. Local connectivity to *.cursorvm.com appears fine; this looks like a stuck cloud Agent Computer on the account side. Please help …\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494502-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494502-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ejust open and found the issue\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-494502-screenshots-screen-recordings-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-494502-screenshots-screen-recordings-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eScreenshots / Screen Recordings\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/5/e/5e16b6e15de7e6887abb85852245343dcc0d61bb.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/dqlxWMgEYEB4Dk79Ga5D4c5j4wP.png?dl=1\" ti